    "function:rack::simd::clamp(rack::simd::float_4, rack::simd::float_4, rack::simd::float_4)": {
      "finding": "P2: the float_4 overload's docstring says 'fmin(fmax(x, a), b) per lane: a wins if b < a' (native/bindings/simd/functions.cpp:129-130), but Rack's float_4 clamp is fmin(fmax(x, a), b) (Rack-SDK include/simd/functions.hpp, 'inline float_4 clamp'), so when b < a the result is b: fmax(x, a) >= a > b, then fmin(..., b) = b. Only the scalar math::clamp returns a (math.hpp:104-107, std::fmax(std::fmin(x, b), a)). The binding calls Rack correctly and the reference cases match; only the help text is wrong. Smallest fix: change the docstring to 'b wins if b < a (unlike the scalar math::clamp, where a wins)' and optionally note this difference in docs/reference/simd.md#simd-functions.",
      "verdict": "finding"
    },
